# Window geometry.
#
# default_border pixel: no title bars, just a 2px edge. Affordable now that
# waybar's centre module shows the focused window's title - the title bar had
# become redundant chrome repeating what the bar already says.
#
# smart_gaps: a lone window on a workspace gets no gap, so a single maximised
# terminal is not framed by dead space.
default_border pixel 2
# Floating windows match the tiled ones rather than keeping title bars. The
# title bar was also the drag handle, but $mod+drag already moves a floating
# window, so nothing is actually lost.
default_floating_border pixel 2
gaps inner 6
smart_gaps on

##client.focused #7a5ada #7a5ada #ffff00
# Five arguments, not three: <border> <background> <text> <indicator>
# <child_border>. `child_border` is the border drawn around the window itself -
# i.e. what you actually see with `default_border pixel` - and when omitted it
# silently inherits <background>. With three arguments the focused window drew
# a BLACK child_border (#000000, the old titlebar background) and the unfocused
# one #333333, so once title bars were dropped there was no visible focus
# indicator at all on a dark wallpaper.
#
# #2c78bf is the same blue waybar uses for the focused workspace, so the two
# "this has focus" signals match rather than being two unrelated colours.
#
# <indicator> is the 4th and was never set either: it marks the edge where the
# next window will open in a tiled container.
client.focused #2c78bf #000000 #9f9f9f #2c78bf #2c78bf
client.unfocused #333333 #333333 #666666 #333333 #333333
client.focused_inactive #45347b #45347b #aaaaaa #45347b #45347b
client.urgent #D11931 #D11931 #ffffff #D11931 #D11931

